 - **Blaster** (f0100): eating a ghost has a chance of granting one blaster shot (default 50%, a tuning constant to set after a Beta playtest); at most three are held and a drop while holding three is wasted; firing spends one; a hit ghost behaves exactly like an eaten one (the next value in the chain, eyes home, harmless until it has revived). The shot is two-dimensional along the maze grid, the way the player looks, rounded to the nearest heading (the arrows' direction when one is held). The roll is seeded on the server. The power pellet stays as it is. **(prep)**: the blaster works any time in play; a miss is spent; the shot is instant along its row or column, stopped by walls, doors and the house, carried round the side tunnel once; the first active ghost on the line is hit (eyes and ghosts in the house are passed through); only a contact eat rolls for a drop; the chain also restarts when the power runs out; shots outlive a death and a level and are gone on a new run; a fire in a pause does nothing; the shot starts from the tile the server has the player on before that step's move, with no grace, so with ordinary latency (about 100 ms round trip) a shot into a side corridor must be pressed about half a tile before the junction's centre as the player sees it; the drops follow the session seed (the player's user id today), so a player's n-th eaten ghost rolls the same in every game; the HUD shows one cyan bar per shot after the lives, on touch too, where the FIRE button fires them (f0110); a shot the server took shows a short cyan beam.
 - **Spy hop** (f0101): slightly lower walls, ghosts keep the walls' old height (10) and stand above them, and a jump raises the camera over the walls for a short time with a short cooldown; the rail goes on underneath. **Jumping over ghosts** (user, 2026-10-21): "we want to be able to jump to look around, AND to jump over ghosts". The player is airborne only while the eye is above the wall tops (the middle of the jump), and while airborne no ghost catches them, a blue ghost is passed over and not eaten, and pellets passed over are not eaten; the cooldown stays 0.5 s. **(prep)**: walls 9 studs; the eye rises 14 studs and lands in 12 steps (800 ms of real time); airborne the 2nd to the 11th step of it (667 ms; each step judged at its middle). The step rule is off the drawn eye by at most 0.19 of a step, in the player's favour; the next jump 8 steps (533 ms) after landing. The server decides the hop (the `Hop` intent) and the camera shows it.
+- **Waiting at the top** (f0234; the user may veto the prep choices): while a READY pause runs (the run's start, each new life, and, by prep's choice, each new level and a new run) the eye is held at the top of a hop (14 studs up, over the walls), free to look, and lands down the last half of an ordinary hop's arc (6 steps, 400 ms), standing again exactly when play starts. **(prep)**: it is the camera's only; the server decides nothing new (no hop, nothing airborne, the pause unchanged), so the jumps boon's long hop does not lengthen the landing, and the look is left where the player put it when play starts.
 - **Glows** (f0102): the edge arrows give way to glows in eight places on the screen (the edges' middles and the corners), coloured as the ghost, in its direction from where the camera looks, and brighter as it nears; the radar stays. **(prep)**: every ghost within 12 tiles along the maze glows, in view or not (eyes excepted); the nearest in a direction lights it; a glow is at most 12% of the screen's smaller side, in the device's safe area, under the radar, the overlays and the HUD.
 - **Keys**: see *Desktop keys* (f0104). **(prep)**: the arrow look turns at the camera's turn rate and springs back the same way; two arrows that tie aim the way of travel.
 
